--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
kev  (vendored subset)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:  https://github.com/jaredpalmer/kev
Commit:  90990a5fac2995b9faa3190f7d437e84f2067768  (2026-09-21)
License: Apache License 2.0
Author:  Jared Palmer

Vendored verbatim, with NO local modifications, into
src/decis/engines/_kev_vendor/:

  kev/model.py       -> encode(), branch_mask_batch(), PointerHead, DecisionModel
  kev/checkpoint.py  -> Checkpoint, Meta, LoadOptions
  LICENSE            -> the Apache-2.0 text, as required by section 4(a)/(d)

The full licence text is at src/decis/engines/_kev_vendor/LICENSE. The sha256 of
each vendored file is recorded in src/decis/engines/_kev_vendor/VENDOR.md and is
checked by tests/test_kev_vendor.py, so "were these files modified?" is answerable
without diffing against upstream.

kev/api.py is deliberately NOT vendored: Decis implements the wire contract in
src/decis/schema.py + src/decis/answers.py so that every engine shares one answer
and one confidence definition. kev/serve.py (its HTTP layer) and its training,
evaluation and dataset modules are not used either. See VENDOR.md for the rationale
and for the two os.environ reads that exist in the vendored copy.

